sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant APIGateway as Kong Gateway
    participant PatientSvc as Patient Service
    participant AppointmentSvc as Appointment Service
    participant PrescriptionSvc as Prescription Service
    participant BillingSvc as Billing Service
    participant RabbitMQ
    participant Redis

    Client->>APIGateway: 1. Request (POST /appointments)
    APIGateway->>AppointmentSvc: 2. Route to Appointment Service
    AppointmentSvc->>Redis: 3. Check cache
    Redis-->>AppointmentSvc: 4. Cache miss
    AppointmentSvc->>PatientSvc: 5. Verify patient exists (REST)
    PatientSvc-->>AppointmentSvc: 6. Patient found
    AppointmentSvc->>AppointmentSvc: 7. Create appointment
    AppointmentSvc->>RabbitMQ: 8. Publish 'appointment.created' event
    RabbitMQ->>BillingSvc: 9. Forward event
    BillingSvc->>BillingSvc: 10. Generate invoice
    BillingSvc->>RabbitMQ: 11. Publish 'invoice.created' event
    RabbitMQ->>AppointmentSvc: 12. Forward event (if subscribed)
    AppointmentSvc->>Redis: 13. Update cache
    AppointmentSvc-->>APIGateway: 14. Return response
    APIGateway-->>Client: 15. 201 Created

    Note over BillingSvc,RabbitMQ: Asynchronous event processing<br/>(non-blocking)
